    "created_at": "2025-06-28T14:01:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-28T14:11:28Z",
    "body": "Recently I discovered a similar issue in my web project, but with GPUParticles3D.\nIt happened only in the web, that the game froze for almost a minute, after removing these particles it loaded very quickly again.\n\nI found another bug report regarding GPUParticles3D and web, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107633, but this one looks very close, except that I used GPUParticles3D\nI haven't looked into it deeper, if a certain setting causes the problem, or if it happens with GPUParticles3D in general.\n\nAnyway, I uploaded a MRP here as well, I wasn't sure If I should make an own bug report, as it seems so close.\nThis project features the original particle system I used in the game and tested it separated in this project.\n[GPUParticles3D_web_MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20961165/GPUParticles3D_web_MRP.zip)",
