    "created_at": "2026-11-01T23:42:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-06T05:52:28Z",
    "body": "Same with GPUParticles3D on 4.7.2-stable (Compatibility, Chrome on Windows through ANGLE/D3D11). Four GPUParticles3D systems with simple ParticleProcessMaterials (box emission, gravity, turbulence, colour ramp, 26 to 140 particles each) cost 22 to 25 s of compile + link each on a cold load, about 93 s together, timed to the first `LINK_STATUS` query. Each process program had a ~34k character fragment shader containing the attractor and collider loops (`i < attractor_count`, `i < collider_count`); I suspect ANGLE's D3D compiler unrolls those to their maximum, but I did not isolate it. Converting the same systems with `CPUParticles3D.convert_from_particles()` removed the cost completely.\n\nIf it helps, I can build a template with those loops compiled out and measure whether they are the cost, or test a proposed fix on the web side.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
